Included Files (important user-side scripts marked by *):


---
General Tools:

* cz_tools.py
Collection of valuable helper tools for working with Flash AMR and particle data.
(If you need to load or convert anything Flash-related look here first!)

* cl_objcol.py
Scripts for creating column density maps from Flash AMR data.
Can be used on regions or the entire domain.
(Includes plotting routines)

* pt_samplesph.py
Script for SPH-sampling the density field of either a region or the entire simulation domain.
Outputs a particle file that can be used for initializing tracer particles by means of the from_file initmethod.

* automov.py
Automation Script using ffmpeg for combining sets of plots into videos

cz_selfgrav.py
Scripts used to calculate self-gravity and/or external gravity of cell selections from AMR data.
Mainly useful for quantifying tidal interactions.

constants.py
Contains physical constants and units used by other scripts

var_settings_v3.py
Used to hold parameters used when plotting certain variables through other scripts.
Useful for getting consistent scaling settings, units, and value ranges when plotting stuff from multiple other scripts.
(Review/Edit if plots seem to show wrong range)

sinkpart.py
Helper tools for opening and working with flash sink particle data as contained in plotfiles.

---
Object detection:

* cl_find_182.py
Main object finder script for finding clouds / clumps / cores / dendrogram nodes in a flash plotfile. 

cl_dendrofind.py
Scripts used for creating conventional uniform-grid dendrograms through converting back and forth from AMR data.

cz_astrodendro.py
Scripts used for creating dendrograms through directly running astrodendro on AMR-based data 

cl_fellwalk.py
Scripts for using the Fellwalker algorithm directly on AMR grids to find objects (e.g. cores).
(Usually controlled from cl_find)

cl_fofg_142.py
Scripts for finding objects defined through connected spaces satisfying a freely defined set of conditions,
based on Neighbours-of-Neighbours (think Friends-of-Friends but for AMR data instead of SPH).
Useful for finding e.g. molecular clouds and clumps.
(Usually controlled from cl_find)

cl_gaussfit.py
Scripts for finding objects through fitting gaussians to AMR grid data.
(Usually controlled from cl_find)

cz_findfragment.py
Helper scripts for filtering dendrogram nodes by collapse indicators. 


---
Reverse tracking for finding zoom region candidates:

* cl_centertracks_17b.py
Main script for running Euler-integration style reverse object tracking for finding zoom-worthy objects.
(Creates object position tables, plots, and refinement statistic graphs)


---
Hierachical dendrogram tracking though tracer particles:

* cz_trfrag_catalog.py
Pre-compute graph structure from tracking over a list of multiple file
by combining the node event labels found through cz_trfrag.
Marks e.g. identity continuations, splits, mergers, and resegmentations of dendrogram nodes.
(Saves graph for use in other scripts)

* cz_trfragstat150.py
Pre-compute a wide set of statistics for each dendrogram node.
(Saves values for use in other scripts, no plotting routine included)

* pl_trfrag_vst.py
Create plots following the evolution of tracked objects.
(Works on rudimentary level, but no nice plots yet)

cz_tracerown.py
Helper Scripts for figuring out containment and ownership relations
for cell-based objects (e.g. dendrogram nodes), tracer particles, sink particles,
and combinations of the former.

cz_tracermatch.py
Helper Scripts for calculating the scores used for matching tracer sets with each other. 

cz_trfrag.py
Helper Script containing the decision tree for mapping tracer matching scores from
the dendrogram nodes of two consecutive plotfiles onto node event labels.
(Saves events labels for each pair of consecutive plotfiles for use in graph building routine)


---
Library Tools:

libmf/micflash.py
Interface routine for anything regarding the Flash AMR data,
including taks related to reconstructing/querying the underlying octree structure.

libmf/micvar.py
Interface layer for reading data stored in Flash plotfile.
Holds formulae and provides recursive resolver which can be used for calculating 
fields that can be derived from flash data.
( Usually used through interface in micflash.py.
  Use LoadPlotfile in cz_tools for loading the 'leafdata' and 'octree' variables used
  all over the other scripts.
  leafdata is the wrapper for working on plotfile data and derived quantities, e.g.
  leafdata['dens'] returns the density field of all cells of the leaf blocks,
  while leafdata['mass'] contains the gas mass contained in the grid cells.
  Data shape: (lbl,iz,iy,ix), where lbl enumerates the leaf blocks,
  while iz,iy,ix enumerate the cells of the selected blocks in the z-,y-,x-directions.
  Leaf block indicies can be converted to whole-grid block indicies through the
  leafdata.nodeid() member function.
  )

libmf/micplot.py
Automation tools for simplifying plotting tasks connected to flash data.

libmf/rpnparser.py
Helper tool for reading in and resolving formulae given in RPN format (Reversed polish notation).
Used in micvar.py, but also very useful otherwise.
Note that the parser for handling string tokens can be loaded from an external function.
( Fun part: You can build a recursively resolving algebra system from there:
  1.) Bind the rpnparser to a getter function (the one evaluating thingy[...] )
  2.) Loop that getter function back into the string token parser
  )
( In principle, it is also possible to build a system from here that
  resolves conventional-style formulae: "Simply' use the Shunting yard algorithm
  for casting the arithmetical expression into RPN form. (Be warned:
  Implementing Shunting Yard is easy, but extracting the input tokens from
  a continuous input string is stuff of nightmares.
  )

